{
 "Apex-6 is a Blueprinter mod for Nuclear Option 0.34.2. Apex-6 is the smaller drone; Apex-8 is the larger aircraft drone. Both use optical guidance and low radar and infrared signatures.": [
  "Apex-6.dll.17012.unity3d"
 ],
 "The available carriers are the original six-drone Apex-6 TEL, a separate four-drone Apex-8 TEL, an eight-drone Apex-6 cargo pallet, a four-drone Apex-8 cargo pallet, and the Apex-8 aircraft single rail. Internal identifiers for the existing aircraft drone and single rail remain unchanged for compatibility.": [
  "Apex-6.dll.17012.unity3d"
 ],
 "Both pallets use the native cargo ramp and parachute. The release sequence begins seven seconds after the pallet exits the ramp, then ejects one drone every 0.8 seconds. The eight-drone pallet completes its salvo at 12.6 seconds, and the four-drone pallet at 9.4 seconds. Targets and their global coordinates are captured when the player releases the pallet and distributed in order, cycling through the selection when needed. Native optical guidance follows each assigned unit, and the missile owner ID remains the releasing aircraft's ID for damage credit. The empty frame disappears one second aft": [
  "Apex-6.dll.17012.unity3d"
 ],
 "er touching terrain or water; if it lands before the salvo is complete, cleanup waits for the final release. Only the server spawns drones and removes the pallet.": [
  "Apex-6.dll.17012.unity3d"
 ],
 "Pallet drones launch toward their assigned target at 35 degrees above the horizon with a 55 m/s ejection speed. They exit beyond the frame's diagonal envelope, and their starting position is at least 3 m above sea level. The pallet's downward velocity is excluded from the launch velocity so it cannot cancel the initial climb. The parachute frame stays upright while the drone receives the upward launch attitude.": [
  "Apex-6.dll.17012.unity3d"
 ],
 "te and multiplayer behavior still require a mission test.": [
  "Apex-6.dll.17012.unity3d"
 ],
 "Both variants have a configured engagement limit of 137 km. The actual aircraft cruise speed and full-distance flight still need an in-game test. The aircraft model is 2.74 m wide at its current prefab scale, uses its five corresponding FBX materials, and is also displayed on the ready aircraft rail. The aircraft motor uses 4400 N thrust and a 560 s burn, with no hard speed clamp. The aircraft heat haze is placed behind its nozzle.": [
  "Apex-6.dll.17012.unity3d"
 ],
 "The TEL retains its six-rail load, detachable one-second booster, and ammunition display logic. The published DLL includes an embedded Blueprinter bundle; rebuild that bundle after changing these Unity assets, then rebuild the DLL. See the public repository for installation instructions and aircraft hardpoints.": [
  "Apex-6.dll.17012.unity3d"
 ],
 "\"description\": \"A duel between two light carriers; the Cursor-class LFD of BDF and the Devotion-class Escort Carrier of PALA. Both carriers start with their full respective air wings and do not get resupplies.\",": [
  "Aryx.Naval.Expansion_1.0.4.dll.17296.unity3d"
 ],
 "The Andromeda-class Aviation Missile Cruiser is a hulking heavy cruiser designed to sidestep treaties regarding high tonnage carriers on the Mainland's straits, and for the BDF to equalise the playing field in the large surface combatant role against PALA's Dynamo-class. This massive cruiser is armed with two 203mm deck guns and is able to launch huge AGM-99 volleys and lock down airspace with its long-range R-9 SAMs, and launch V/STOVL aircraft to attain air superiority. It is heavily armoured and can hold its own against larger groups of vessels. Once the Strategic threshold is reached, it c": [
  "Aryx.Naval.Expansion_1.0.4.dll.17296.unity3d"
 ],
 "an launch a devastating wave of SLND-9 nuclear missiles at high value targets.": [
  "Aryx.Naval.Expansion_1.0.4.dll.17296.unity3d"
 ],
 "Coming in at 20,000 tonnes and common with mid-tier regional powers on a budget, the Helion-class is amongst the smallest aircraft carriers in the world, and amongst the few capital ships available on the export market. This light carrier is built on the same hull as the Devotion-class albeit equipped with a CATOBAR facelift, sporting two steam catapults on a flat deck and improved defences. It is well defended with 56 RAM-45 anti-air missiles, two IRM-S2 launcher turrets, two 30mm CIWS and an 80kW laser defence system. It can handle a range of aircraft thanks to its catapults and offers arres": [
  "Aryx_FS-41.Eclipse_1.1.7.1.dll.112948.unity3d"
 ],
 "ted landing capability with three wires to the stern.": [
  "Aryx_FS-41.Eclipse_1.1.7.1.dll.112948.unity3d"
 ],
 "At 309m length and displacing over 100,000 tonnes, the Penumbra-class is the largest aircraft carrier ever constructed by a non-superpower nation. The BDF's flagship carrier features a myriad of defences, three water-cooled electro-magnetic aircraft catapults, four arresting wires and three elevators. This colossal vessel": [
  "Aryx_FS-41.Eclipse_1.1.7.1.dll.112948.unity3d"
 ],
 "s trimaran design maximises hangar space, internal volume and beam whilst providing stability in rough seas.": [
  "Aryx_FS-41.Eclipse_1.1.7.1.dll.112948.unity3d"
 ],
 "According to all known laws of aviation and annoying people on the subreddit, there is no way that an MC-260 Chimera should be able to fly. Its little wings are far too small to get its fat little body off of the ground. The Chimera of course, flies anyway, because Aryx doesn't care what aerodynamics thinks.": [
  "Aryx_MC260_Chimera_1.2.0.dll.84708.unity3d"
 ],
 "A short ranged missile, consisting of 6 cluster Active Radar homing bomblets that self-propel themselves towards their targets.": [
  "Bote_1.5.2.dll.62156.unity3d"
 ],
 "The missile is hot-launched and orientates itself in the direction of the threat, and deploys the bomblets.": [
  "Bote_1.5.2.dll.62156.unity3d"
 ],
 "Various systems for deploying cargo and support equipment": [
  "Bote_1.5.2.dll.62156.unity3d"
 ],
 "\"description\": \"Learn how to use flares to defeat IR missiles. For this lesson you will be piloting the T/A-30 Compass trainer aircraft.\",": [
  "resources.assets"
 ],
 "\"body\": \"Flare effectiveness is determined by your aspect to the missile, as well as your engine output. Lower your throttle and turn the plane side-on to the threat to get the most out of your flares. If you get fired on from behind at full throttle, or you may need to expend the whole cartridge.\",": [
  "resources.assets"
 ],
 "\"body\": \"You are pulling away too soon. While the best and most obvious survival method is to avoid the SAM in the first place, for the sake of this demonstration, please take unreasonable risk.\",": [
  "resources.assets"
 ],
 "\"body\": \"Now leave the SAM's area of effect and return to where you started. Because you'll be showing it your exhaust as you fly away, it is especially important that you reduce your throttle to reduce your signature compared to that of your flares.\",": [
  "resources.assets"
 ],
